<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Merged into the generated bundle Info.plist by the Tauri bundler, which looks for a
       file named Info.plist beside tauri.conf.json (tauri-utils config: "Note that Tauri
       also looks for a `Info.plist` file in the same directory as the Tauri configuration
       file"). No tauri.conf.json reference is needed.

       Be clear about what these buy: a purpose string changes the sentence macOS shows
       INSIDE a privacy dialog. It does not remove a single prompt. Ingest Pilot shipped
       with none of them, which is why every prompt the user saw was bare system text with
       no explanation of what the app wanted or why. Reducing the NUMBER of prompts is the
       job of not walking the startup disk (see scanner::is_on_system_disk).

       Deliberately absent: a string for kTCCServiceSystemPolicyAppData ("would like to
       access data from other apps"). Apple exposes no Info.plist key for that service, so
       it cannot be explained here — the only fix is to never read another app's container,
       which is what skipping ~/Library in is_skipped_directory does. -->

  <key>NSRemovableVolumesUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Ingest Pilot reads the camera cards and external drives you connect so it can copy, verify, and catalogue your footage.</string>

  <key>NSNetworkVolumesUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Ingest Pilot needs this to copy footage to or from a server or NAS you have chosen as a source or destination.</string>

  <key>NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Ingest Pilot reads or writes your Documents folder only when you choose it as an offload destination or as the location for your preset library.</string>

  <key>NSDesktopFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Ingest Pilot reads or writes your Desktop only when you choose it as an offload destination.</string>

  <key>NSDownloadsFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Ingest Pilot reads or writes your Downloads folder only when you choose it as an offload destination.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
